From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:56:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: no self-deadlock on a kickout for a station
 being removed

A peer sta kickout event for a peer whose station mac80211 had already
unlinked called ath11k_dp_peer_cleanup() with ab->base_lock held, and
that takes the lock again: the CE tasklet spun on it forever, the NAPI
thread spun behind it, and the watchdog reset the AP. It hit when a
client moved between the 5 GHz and 6 GHz BSSs of one AP and the old
radio's firmware kicked out the peer it was still deleting (two resets
in two weeks). The same path also read sta and the saved peer
uninitialized when no radio had the peer.

Such a peer is being removed: ath11k_mac_station_remove() cleans up its
receive state and deletes it. Skip it, at debug level.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c | 26 +++++++++++---------------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
index ef97013..c493c2e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
@@ -8222,10 +8222,7 @@ static void ath11k_peer_sta_kickout_event(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct sk_buff
 {
 	struct wmi_peer_sta_kickout_arg arg = {};
 	struct ieee80211_sta *sta;
-	struct ath11k_peer *peer;
-	struct ath11k_peer *save_peer;
 	struct ath11k *ar;
-	struct ath11k *save_ar;
 	int i;
 
 	if (ath11k_pull_peer_sta_kickout_ev(ab, skb, &arg) != 0) {
@@ -8238,27 +8235,26 @@ static void ath11k_peer_sta_kickout_event(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct sk_buff
 	spin_lock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ab->num_radios; i++) {
-		struct ath11k_pdev *pdev = &ab->pdevs[i];
-		ar = pdev->ar;
-		peer = ath11k_peer_find_by_addr(ar, arg.mac_addr);
-		if (!peer) {
+		ar = ab->pdevs[i].ar;
+		if (!ath11k_peer_find_by_addr(ar, arg.mac_addr))
 			continue;
-		}
-		save_peer = peer;
-		save_ar = ar;
+
+		/* A peer whose station mac80211 has already unlinked is being
+		 * removed: ath11k_mac_station_remove() cleans it up and deletes
+		 * it, so a kickout the firmware raced in has nothing to do.
+		 */
 		sta = ieee80211_find_sta_by_ifaddr(ar->hw, arg.mac_addr, NULL);
 		if (!sta) {
-			    continue;
+			ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_WMI,
+				   "peer sta kickout %pM: station being removed\n",
+				   arg.mac_addr);
+			continue;
 		}
 
 		ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_WMI, "event peer sta kickout %pM", arg.mac_addr);
 
 		ieee80211_report_low_ack(sta, 10);
 	}
-	if (!sta && save_peer) {
-		ath11k_warn(ab, "Spurious quick kickout for STA %pM but found in peer table\n", arg.mac_addr);
-		ath11k_dp_peer_cleanup(save_ar, save_peer->vdev_id, arg.mac_addr);
-	}
 
 	spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 	rcu_read_unlock();
